= Waves 10–12 cross-wave audit =

'''State: post-merge cross-wave audit.'''

== Scope ==

This audit covers the three consecutive merged corpus waves completed on 2026-09-19:

* [[BITwiki:Wave 10 context audit|Wave 10 — Decisions, incentives, and collective systems]]: 13 concepts / 39 reader surfaces.
* [[BITwiki:Wave 11 context audit|Wave 11 — Decentralized systems and on-chain market primitives]]: 21 concepts / 63 reader surfaces.
* [[BITwiki:Wave 12 context audit|Wave 12 — Biology and bioinformatics bridge]]: 10 concepts / 30 reader surfaces.

Combined scope:

<pre>
44 canonical concepts
132 reader surfaces
Core + Simple + Technical
</pre>

Overall corpus after Wave 12:

<pre>
203 canonical concepts
609 reader surfaces
</pre>

The audit checks merged <code>main</code>, semantic boundaries, reader-link resolution, evidence/provenance quality, request lifecycle, and completion bookkeeping.

== Audit method ==

The audit re-runs five editorial layers:

# '''Structural / identity''' — one Core identity per concept; derivative Simple/Technical surfaces remain identity/category-exempt.
# '''Semantic boundaries''' — adjacent concepts must not become aliases merely because they interact.
# '''Knowledge-graph resolution''' — reader-facing Core links are checked against canonical Main-space identities; future coverage signals must not masquerade as existing canonical dependencies.
# '''Evidence / provenance''' — current standards/drafts are labeled by actual publication state.
# '''Workflow / bookkeeping''' — satisfied knowledge requests and merged-wave ledger state must agree with the canonical corpus.

